OL,3,GNEWSAAge UK in-person service to close
OL,4,Ain a few weeks
OL,5,
OL,6,FA charity which provides dementia
OL,7,Fservices in the East Grinstead area is
OL,8,Fdue to close its in-person premises at
OL,9,Fthe end of the month, it has been
OL,10,Fconfirmed.
OL,12,FAge UK West Sussex, Brighton and Hove
OL,13,Fwill no longer be based at the Glen Vue
OL,14,FCentre, as Age UK says attendance is
OL,15,F"low on some days" in a building that
OL,16,Fhas "become increasingly expensive to
OL,17,Frun".
OL,19,FAmong those affected is the family of
OL,20,FOliver Tully, whose 88-year-old father
OL,21,Fhas been attending the dementia club
OL,22,Fthree days a week.
OL,23,APub: 11-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,329,320,200,140,0,100
